From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:20:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: stop a spike download part way, to see what the vault
 keeps

The loopback server can leave a blob's length out, send it no faster
than a rate, and answer a Range with the rest of a sized blob, as a
server that lets a download resume does. A client that goes away no
longer throws on the server's thread, where it would have killed the
app. The gate can pause or cancel a download it queued, then try it
again, through the broadcasts its notification's buttons send; it logs
each status the download passes through, and lists what the vault holds
of the spike's writes. Its comment named a script that never existed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
